    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are a base class and a helper), and it's now green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response to include a derived `membershipTier` field: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 **and** an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nI followed the existing pattern for read-only derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`), which are declared in the OpenAPI schema and computed in the MapStruct mapper:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto` and a `membershipTier(Owner)` default method that returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and email is non-blank, else `\"BRONZE\"`. Null-safety on `namesakeCount`/`email` keeps it robust for any owner lacking those values (falls through to `BRONZE`).\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full `mvn test` build pass green.",
